{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "ddfc745f-0735-54b6-9f50-75973008868d",
		"name": "Ch 12 - Log In Once (auto token)",
		"description": "# Log in once, reuse the token\n\nThe collection uses **Bearer Token** `{{token}}`, and every request inherits it. The collection pre-request script logs in only when `token` is missing or about to expire, and stores the new token and its expiry time in collection variables.\n\nBefore you send: start the practice API (`node server.js` in the practice-api folder) and select the environment **Practice API - Local** in the environment selector at the top right.\n\nTo watch it renew the token, set the collection variable `tokenLifetime` to `10` (seconds).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Who am I",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
